 L58: \nL59: cite27†Get Access L60: \nL61: cite28†BibTeX L62: \nL63: cite0†Tools L64: ## Abstract\nL65: \nL66: If the absolute value of a (real) polynomial of degree d is bounded by 1 at k equally spaced points of the real line, it is of interest to know how large its absolute value on the interval spanned by the points can be. This work provides a fairly definitive answer to this question.\nL67: \nL68: ### MSC codes\nL69: \nL70:   1. cite29†26C05 L71: \nL72: ### Keywords\nL73: \nL74:   1. cite30†polynomials L75:   2. cite31†comparison of norms L76: ## Get full access to this article\nL77: \nL78: View all available purchase options and get full access to this article.\nL79: \nL80: cite27†Get Access L81: \nL82: Already a Subscriber? Sign in as an cite32†individual†sso.siam.org or via your cite33†institution L83: ## References\nL84: \nL85: 1.\nL86: \nL87: H. Ehlich, K. Zeller, Schwankung von Polynomen zwischen Gitterpunkten, Math. Z., 86 (1964), 41–44\nL88: \nL89: cite34†Crossref†doi.org L90: \nL91: cite35†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L92: \nL93: 2.\nL94: \nL95: Hartmut Ehlich, Karl Zeller, Numerische Abschätzung von Polynomen, Z. Angew. Math. Mech., 45 (1965), T20–T22\nL96: \nL97: cite36†Crossref†doi.org L98: \nL99: cite37†Web of Science†gateway.webofknowledge.com L100: \nL101: cite38†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L102: \nL103: 3.\nL104: \nL105: Hartmut Ehlich, Polynome zwischen Gitterpunkten, Math. Z., 93 (1966), 144–153\nL106: \nL107: cite39†Crossref†doi.org L108: cite40†Web of Science†gateway.webofknowledge.com L109: \nL110: cite41†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L111: \nL112: 4.\nL113: \nL114: A. Schönhage, Fehlerfortpflanzung bei Interpolation, Numer. Math., 3 (1961), 62–71\nL115: \nL116: cite42†Crossref†doi.org L117: \nL118: cite43†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L119: ## Information & Authors\nL120: \nL121: ### Information\nL122: \nL123: #### Published In\nL124: \nL125: cite44†Image: cover